    "text": "Your 1.1GB Node image and your cache miss on every single push are the same bug: you put the thing that changes most at the bottom of the stack. This handbook walks the actual mechanics — union filesystem layers, whiteout files that keep deleted bytes shipping forever, what really goes into a cache key, and why `rm -rf` in a later RUN saves you exactly zero megabytes. Ten pages, ending at 150MB with a non-root user and pinned digests.",
